# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template README tells you to copy. `.env*` above swallowed it, so a
# fresh clone had nothing to copy and setup failed at step one.
!.env.local.example

# Claude Code local settings — per-machine tool permissions, including absolute
# scratchpad paths. Ignored by this machine's global gitignore too, but that does not
# travel with a clone, and this repo is meant to go public.
.claude/settings.local.json

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# job-copilot
/data/
.env.local
.env

# Personal profile data — contact details and a private target-company list.
# Committed templates live alongside as *.example.*; copy them and fill in locally.
/profile/resume_base.md
/profile/profile.toml

# Generated application artifacts — regenerate with scripts/tailor.ts + scripts/to-docx.ts.
# These carry the user's phone, email, and (in *-answers.md) salary posture, so none of it
# is ever committed.
#
# /resumes/ is where they live: one directory holding a job's JD, tailored .md, answers and
# .docx, instead of a littered repo root. Ignored whole, so it does not exist in a fresh
# clone — lib/outfile.ts creates it on first write rather than failing after the LLM call.
/resumes/
#
# The root-level rules stay as a backstop, because --out still accepts any path and a single
# stray `--out tailored.md` is a résumé with a phone number in it committed to a public repo.
# This is an ALLOWLIST, not a pattern match: every root-level .md/.docx/.txt is treated as
# generated output unless named below. Filename-convention patterns (/tailored*.md) were
# tried first and leaked — real files got named after the company/role and matched nothing.
/*.md
/*.docx
/*.txt
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# Throwaway probe scripts. A one-off query against lib/store.ts has to run from INSIDE the
# repo — Node resolves imports from the script's own directory, so the same file under
# /tmp cannot see node_modules and fails on both "./lib/store" and "jszip". AGENTS.md tells
# you to write it here and delete it; this makes forgetting harmless rather than a commit.
/*.probe.ts

# Playwright: fixture DB + run output
/tests/ui/.tmp/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/.playwright/
